2026/06/12 11:04:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.mipro_optimizer_v2: 0: Based on the main theme of given the news article, categorize it into World, Sports, Business, or Tech.

2026/06/12 11:04:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.mipro_optimizer_v2: 1: You are a newsroom-style text classification assistant. Your task is to read a short news blurb (1–2 sentences, wire-service style) and assign a single category label from the set: World, Sports, Business, Tech. Use the content of the blurb to determine the topic, paying attention to datelines, attributions, named entities, and events. Respond with only the chosen label (e.g., Sports, Business) in title case. Do not provide explanations or additional text.

2026/06/12 11:04:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.mipro_optimizer_v2: 2: You are a concise news topic classifier. Given a single input Text (a news blurb), assign one of the predefined labels: World, Sports, Business, or Tech. Base your decision on the dominant topic cues in the text (e.g., international events for World, sports events/teams for Sports, financial/market activity for Business, technology/products/industry for Tech). Return only the chosen label as a plain string with no extra text or formatting. If the category is ambiguous, choose the label that best fits the main focus of the piece and remain consistent with the provided examples.

2026/06/12 11:04:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.mipro_optimizer_v2: 3: Generate a single label from the set {World, Business, Tech, Sports} for the provided short news blurb (typically 1–2 sentences). Use an in-context learning approach: include a few representative News–Label examples in the prompt, then output only the appropriate label for the input text. Do not add any extraneous text or formatting. Rely on the content and topics (e.g., international events for World, markets for Business, technology for Tech, sports events for Sports). If the content is ambiguous, choose the most probable label based on the main subject.

2026/06/12 11:04:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.mipro_optimizer_v2: 4: Classify the provided news Text into one of the four categories: World, Sports, Business, or Tech. Use the article’s content to determine the correct category, relying on explicit topics such as geopolitical events for World, athletic events for Sports, markets/companies/finances for Business, and technology/science/IT topics for Tech. If the category is unclear, choose the closest match based on the strongest cues in the text. Output only the exact label: World, Sports, Business, or Tech (no extra words or punctuation).

2026/06/12 11:04:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.mipro_optimizer_v2: 5: Create a concise, deterministic classifier prompt that, given a single news snippet text, outputs exactly one category from the set {World, Business, Tech, Sports}. Do not include any extraneous text or formatting in the output—only the chosen label. If the snippet mentions multiple topics or is ambiguous, prioritize the main topic implied by the content, and ensure consistency with the four-category taxonomy (World, Business, Tech, Sports). The prompt should support few-shot examples if provided, but always return only the label for the input snippet.

